{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1516199-raising-the-yamato-how-to-handle","id":1516199,"title":"Raising the Yamato ...how to handle","path":["Home","Onyx Path","Onyx Path Worlds","Scion"],"posts":[{"date":"2023-06-26T04:48:29-07:00","id":1516199,"title":"Raising the Yamato ...how to handle","content":"This is one I had proposed by my players last night and was a bit unexpected to say the least.. They are doing it to build ties to mortal governments and intuitions, as well as a diplomatic in with the Kami.<br /> <br /> I'm already considering the various mortal reactions. I definitely think this is a Deed worthy of Legend.<br /> <br /> I'm trying to think of complications arising from this but am a bit fuzzy this morning, Suggestions are welcome<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13091-thewanderingjewels","name":"TheWanderingJewels","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13091_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"112"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-27T10:34:33-07:00","id":1516352,"title":"","content":"There is a real-life effort by the LDP to get government funding to raise the Yamato. There was even a 3d survey done of the site to study the feasibility. So, IMHO, the best way to handle it would be for a scion to patron the cause and use social marvels to make raising it a cultural necessity.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12488-jeremysbrain","name":"Jeremysbrain","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"209"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-28T09:10:27-07:00","id":1516467,"title":"","content":"Ok, so regarding complications, i see two kind that could arise. One fairly classic, the other a little bit more problematic.<br /> <br /> The first one would be the good old Titan's interference. Raising the shipwreck of the Yamato would necessarily involve aquatic shenanigans, which means that Namazu could be involved, by trying to infliltrate the expedition with her pawns (or Spawns) to derail it into her advantage (aka, her liberation). Another twist could be that the Yamato, being at the bottom of the Pacific Ocean, is now the property of none other than \u00c1o Guang, the Great Blue Dragon of the East (not to be confused with the real dragon Ryujin, though he could also get into this mess). As described in the book &quot;Titanomachy&quot;, he is not keen on thieves who takes away his stuff without his permission. Maybe he has even transformed the all thing into a palace for his aquatic minions.<br /> <br /> The second type of complications is a bit more a can of worms. The Yamato was afterall the flagship of the Japanese Imperial Navy at the start of the war with the US : it's a heavy symbol, both good and bad. By using it, you are touching the quite complicated case of the Kami and WW2 in the World of Scion. Based on what we can read in the book &quot;Heroes&quot;, the conflict divided the Pantheon between those who condemned it (aka, Amaterasu, who decided after it that she needed to maintain an Incarnation at the japanese imperial court at all time to avoid further problems) and those who first supported it, but are now regreting there actions (aka Bishamon, who became appaled by the atrocities in China, so much so that he is one of the rare Gods in Scion willing to change his Mantle into a more protective one). And that's just the two who have active lore regarding this subject ! Who knows are the other Fortunes reacted, or the involvement of Takemikazuchi and Hachiman during the conflict.<br /> <br /> My point is, if you are willing to touch on this heavy subject, one source of complications could well be the Kami themselves, at least, some of them who are very pleased that the past remains buried into the ocean. It could be interesting that your Scions are negociating peacefully and in friendly terms with the very gods and goddesses who are trying to sabotage their attempt. Plus, it would be a good illustration of the duality of the Kami's virtues. But again, it's a heavy and sensitive subjetc, so be careful using it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Sorry i am french ;__;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27418-lady-darcia","name":"Lady Darcia","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27418_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-29T13:42:30-07:00","id":1516688,"title":"","content":"And pantheons, whose peoples suffered at the hands of Japanese imperialism are not going to look on such a thing kindly. The Shen of China, the Atua of Polynesia, the Tengri of Mongolia, and the Bahala of the Visayas (an indigenous people of the Philippines, forthcoming in <i>God</i>) all will most likely see this as deeply offensive--and those are just from the published pantheons.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26114-muskrat","name":"Muskrat","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"75"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-07-07T04:46:11-07:00","id":1517343,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lady Darcia</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1516199-raising-the-yamato-how-to-handle?p=1516467#post1516467\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Ok, so regarding complications, i see two kind that could arise. One fairly classic, the other a little bit more problematic.<br /> <br /> The first one would be the good old Titan's interference. Raising the shipwreck of the Yamato would necessarily involve aquatic shenanigans, which means that Namazu could be involved, by trying to infliltrate the expedition with her pawns (or Spawns) to derail it into her advantage (aka, her liberation). Another twist could be that the Yamato, being at the bottom of the Pacific Ocean, is now the property of none other than \u00c1o Guang, the Great Blue Dragon of the East (not to be confused with the real dragon Ryujin, though he could also get into this mess). As described in the book &quot;Titanomachy&quot;, he is not keen on thieves who takes away his stuff without his permission. Maybe he has even transformed the all thing into a palace for his aquatic minions.<br /> <br /> The second type of complications is a bit more a can of worms. The Yamato was afterall the flagship of the Japanese Imperial Navy at the start of the war with the US : it's a heavy symbol, both good and bad. By using it, you are touching the quite complicated case of the Kami and WW2 in the World of Scion. Based on what we can read in the book &quot;Heroes&quot;, the conflict divided the Pantheon between those who condemned it (aka, Amaterasu, who decided after it that she needed to maintain an Incarnation at the japanese imperial court at all time to avoid further problems) and those who first supported it, but are now regreting there actions (aka Bishamon, who became appaled by the atrocities in China, so much so that he is one of the rare Gods in Scion willing to change his Mantle into a more protective one). And that's just the two who have active lore regarding this subject ! Who knows are the other Fortunes reacted, or the involvement of Takemikazuchi and Hachiman during the conflict.<br /> <br /> My point is, if you are willing to touch on this heavy subject, one source of complications could well be the Kami themselves, at least, some of them who are very pleased that the past remains buried into the ocean. It could be interesting that your Scions are negociating peacefully and in friendly terms with the very gods and goddesses who are trying to sabotage their attempt. Plus, it would be a good illustration of the duality of the Kami's virtues. But again, it's a heavy and sensitive subjetc, so be careful using it.</div> </div> </div> </div>As a History student and having and interest in the Indo-Asian area, I'm have noticed the rather large can of worms from the mortal side of the Equation. I had started my players off in Origins level characters with Iron Levels of general awareness and activity until an initiating event started 'The Weirdness' beginning to openly Manifest. The characters have been responsible for several major saves for locals so their Legend is spreading. But I have had the opposition getting several victories as well.<br /> <br /> In fact, in spite of hint drops from my end, the players ignore several clues which could of helped them stop the victories. And so, one destroyed city later and multiple hamstrings to some of their contacts, they have finally realized that the OpFor's care not for mortal sensitivities. They are here to win. And if that involves stacking bodies like cordwood and pissing people off, so be it.<br /> <br /> But the players have been doing the conciliatory route, and have been getting good results so far. But raising the Yamato is a massive event. I have considered the massive Media event of seeing the Yamato heading for Uraga Dock, so this will prove...interesting<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13091-thewanderingjewels","name":"TheWanderingJewels","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13091_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"112"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}